cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Recall-MCP
message: >-
  If you use Recall-MCP in your work, please cite it using this
  metadata.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Pranam
    family-names: Srivastava
identifier: recall-mcp
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-12"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/pranam/recall-mcp"
abstract: >-
  A local-first semantic memory broker for AI agents. An MCP server
  (stdio + streamable-HTTP) exposing remember/recall/forget/update/
  capture/list tools over one SQLite file, plus a REST API, OpenAPI
  document, Prometheus metrics, a web UI, and a CLI. Retrieval is a
  hybrid of BM25 keyword scoring, embedding cosine similarity, recency
  decay, and pinned boosts, with an explainable score breakdown on
  every result. Optional encryption at rest (ChaCha20-Poly1305 with
  HKDF key separation and keyed FTS token digests).
keywords:
  - mcp
  - model-context-protocol
  - ai-agents
  - memory
  - rust
  - sqlite
  - local-first
